marco_onboard: Hi team — onboarding hit a strange throttle during our first canary. We use the Java SDK v2.1.1 in a container pool (40 short-lived containers). After a deploy warmup (~120 RPS) we started seeing bursts of 429s to /v1/embeddings. This was transient but repeats on each deploy. Any quick mitigation?

tara_cs: Thanks for flagging, Marco. Can you paste the SDK init snippet and whether containers call prefetch on startup or lazily on first request? Also are you using ephemeral creds?

marco_onboard: Long-lived key for now. Init: ```java
RedwoodClient client = RedwoodClient.builder().apiKey(System.getenv("RW_KEY")).build();
// each container calls client.prefetchAuth(); on start
```No splay — pool ramp is rapid during deploys.

lee_eng: Sounds like a preflight stampede across short-lived containers + connection churn. Two fast mitigations: 1) stop eager prefetch on every container start (do lazy first-request prefetch) or add a randomized startup delay 2) enable a client-side token cache so containers reuse tokens if restarted quickly. Also set the HTTP client to reuse connections (keep-alive) and increase max idle connections.

xi_se: Example quick change (Java): ```java
// lazy prefetch
public Response requestWithToken(Request r){
  String t = tokenCache.get();
  if (t==null){
    synchronized(lock){
      if (tokenCache.get()==null) tokenCache.set(client.fetchEphemeral());
    }
  }
  r.addHeader("Authorization", "Bearer "+tokenCache.get());
  return client.execute(r);
}
// client config
HttpClientConfig cfg = new HttpClientConfig().keepAlive(true).maxIdleConnections(16);
```
And add retry-on-429 with exponential backoff + jitter.

feature-bot: temporary_preflight_quota_increase applied for tenant marco_onboard until ts=1776501800.

marco_onboard: Implemented lazy prefetch + synchronized single-flight fetch + keepAlive + maxIdle 16 and a tiny 0-6s jitter on container start. Redeploying now.

lee_eng: Also add a small in-process cache TTL of ~45s so containers reuse tokens across quick restarts. If you can, rotate to ephemeral creds later; ephemeral flow with SDK caching reduces per-start preflight dramatically.

marco_onboard: Post-change: burst 429s dropped from dozens to <3 on first warmup. Sample log: ```log
[1776500045] container/start splay=4.2s
[1776500052] token: cache miss -> fetched
[1776500068] embed:200 latency=210ms
```
Thanks. Can you keep the quota bump for 12h while we run larger canaries and upgrade to v2.1.3?

tara_cs: Yup we left the temporary bump on for 12h. I'll follow up with a one-pager runbook containing recommended flags: lazy prefetch, single-flight token fetch, token_cache_ttl=45s, http.keepAlive=true, http.maxIdleConnections=16, startup_splay=0-8s, retry(backoff+jitter). Also include steps to request a permanent preflight quota increase if you expect many containers to boot simultaneously in production.

xi_se: FYI v2.1.3 has improved single-flight primitives and better default keepalive settings. Ping me if you want help with the upgrade path.

marco_onboard: Will schedule the upgrade. Appreciate the fast help — will paste the postmortem here once the canary finishes. :thumbsup:
